From dc88d36950e241753823963a1c920d976b62b299 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian <219239532+markd3ng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 18:05:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(frontend): zip multi-file and directory uploads

Context:
Issue #83 requires directory, multi-file, and ZIP upload UX on the
current PasteBin uploader. Redesign against this repo only: package
selected files client-side into one ZIP and reuse the existing
upload/encryption/MPU pipeline. No server filesystem, no new API,
no P2P, no new crypto.

Expected behavior:
Two or more files, or a directory picker selection, become one STORE
ZIP paste. Nested webkitRelativePath is preserved after sanitizing
away traversal/absolute/NUL paths. A single ordinary file stays a
normal file upload. Encryption still uses AES-GCM on the resulting
bytes. MPU still applies above 5 MiB.

Acceptance criteria:
- Multiple files become one ZIP named archive.zip.
- Directory selection ZIPs with {dir}.zip and nested relative paths.
- Traversal paths are rejected; empty safe set fails closed.
- Existing single-file and text paste flows remain.
- No extra ZIP dependency.

Constraints:
- Source patch vs pinned upstream 0835cac4ab8f974035d31845f5c2b93b0c85b5c6.
- REVIEW ONLY; do not merge into upstream-sync.
- Residual: in-memory STORE ZIP (uncompressed).

Validation:
- Node v22.23.2 / pnpm 10.28.0
- 23 files / 177 tests PASS
- lint, typecheck, prettier, frontend build, wrangler dry-run PASS

Docs:
- README.md feature bullet
- PasteBin usage line

Refs:
